    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the possible-duplicate (soft-match) rule on `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it is still created and flagged.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted fields `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) with getters/setters, mapped to new columns. These are stored so they're readable via `GET /api/owners/{id}` (which the test does).\n\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `assignPossibleDuplicate(...)`, called from `assignDerivedAttributes` (after the hard-duplicate check passes, before persisting). It scans existing owners for one sharing the candidate's postcode and `lastName` (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed via the existing `normalizeName`) but a different telephone, picking the earliest (lowest id) match. Sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf = <matching id>` when found, otherwise `false`/`null`. A null postcode never matches.\n\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them (MapStruct maps them automatically by name).\n\n- **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` and `possible_duplicate_of` columns.\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`, the only test class) passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
